From 21fbfba5c4d3a2cc77707fea885590479cec18c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:52:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: start out-of-light maneuvers when the light is about to
 burn out

borg_think_dungeon_light()'s entry test was
  !BI_LIGHT && (BI_LIGHT <= 0 || timeout <= 3)
-- once the first clause holds, the second is always true, so the
about-to-burn-out clause (timeout <= 3) never fired on its own: a lit
lantern three turns from dying was left to go dark even with a spare
torch or oil in the pack.

Make the test  (!BI_LIGHT || (timeout <= 3 && !NO_FUEL)): the
fuel-less (everburning) lights keep their timeout permanently at zero
and must not trigger the maneuvers, so the timeout arm only applies to
fueled lights. Owner-facing effect measured natively: a Warrior with a
lit lantern at timeout 3 and a fresh torch in the pack now swaps to
the torch instead of walking into darkness.
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
index 59560f0a0..a0255e4be 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
@@ -149,8 +149,9 @@ bool borg_think_dungeon_light(void)
     if (borg.trait[BI_ISHUNGRY] && borg_use_things())
         return true;
 
-    if (!borg.trait[BI_LIGHT]
-        && (borg.trait[BI_LIGHT] <= 0 || borg_items[INVEN_LIGHT].timeout <= 3)
+    if ((!borg.trait[BI_LIGHT]
+        || (borg_items[INVEN_LIGHT].timeout <= 3
+            && !of_has(borg_items[INVEN_LIGHT].flags, OF_NO_FUEL)))
         && borg.trait[BI_CDEPTH] >= 1) {
         enum borg_need need;
 
